    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.96). **Gunnar Henderson** holds the premier score of the slate, benefiting from a +16% park factor and a favorable platoon matchup against Dustin May. While **Jackson Merrill** faces Tyler Phillips, his elite +13% dynamic platoon boost makes him an essential start. We are also banking on **Kyle Tucker** (70.26) and **Heliot Ramos** (67.57) to provide the necessary power-speed infusion; notably, **Heliot Ramos** receives a rare \"slow delivery\" bonus that elevates his stolen base potential against Eduardo Rodriguez. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.25) remains a pillar in the utility slot, maintaining a strong output despite a neutral-to-slight negative platoon interaction against the velocity profile of Kumar Rocker.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (49.08), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Brayan Rocchio**. While **Sam Antonacci** possesses the profile to contribute, the combination of his L/L platoon disadvantage and the lower-order volatility inherent in our current projections forced him to the pine. We are monitoring **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Lara** closely; as all seven are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status, their final efficiency scores could shift drastically if they drop in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution given the volatility of these mid-tier scorers, but the collective floor remains high enough to sustain our competitive standing.",
